[h1]Rimworld Statistics — Lifetime Statistics Across Saves[/h1]
[b]RimWorld 1.7 / Requires Harmony[/b]

See the history of your RimWorld playthroughs from the title screen, without loading each save one by one.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*]Summary of in-game days, colonies and recorded playtime across your saves
[*]Ending counts, including different ending types
[*]Wealth records and available raid, death, research and other saved statistics
[*]Per-colony numeric details (no charts)
[*]Read-only import of pre-installation save files made with RimWorld 1.5–1.7
[*]Extension framework for third-party mod statistics (optional add-ons are distributed separately)
[/list]

[b]Important limitations[/b]
[list]
[*]Totals are based on available saves and stored profiles. A permanent lifetime ledger retaining all data from deleted or lost saves is not yet implemented.
[*]Events not preserved in older saves cannot be reconstructed. Unknown and partially observed data are not treated as zero.
[*]Additional experimental event tracking is OFF by default. To try selected units, enable them in mod settings and restart RimWorld.
[*]Experimental statistics, compatibility with all mod configurations, and long-session performance have not been fully verified.
[*]Multiple saves of the same colony are not blindly added together. Branches are handled only where supported by evidence.
[/list]

[b]Required mod[/b]
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]

[b]Supported game version[/b]
RimWorld 1.7. Limited reading of old 1.5–1.7 save files does not mean this mod runs on earlier game versions.

